Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.10,0:00:09.54,Default,,0,0,0,,An assistant saying done is not proof. AIGON PROOF gives each action an exact review,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.54,0:00:14.62,Default,,0,0,0,,an authenticated approval, and a receipt for the work actually performed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.99,0:00:21.82,Default,,0,0,0,,First, a client contract is addressed to an external partner. The server knows the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.82,0:00:27.97,Default,,0,0,0,,document contains personal data. It blocks the action. Even an operator cannot
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.97,0:00:29.92,Default,,0,0,0,,approve this policy violation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.88,0:00:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,We explicitly choose the anonymised summary instead. The document and recipient are
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.00,0:00:43.92,Default,,0,0,0,,shown before approval. Nothing in this command invents consent or silently changes
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.92,0:00:45.40,Default,,0,0,0,,the trust boundary.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.52,0:00:52.22,Default,,0,0,0,,The operator unlocks approval with a private credential. That credential is never
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.22,0:00:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,part of the agent's command or passport.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.63,0:01:03.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Approve once records who approved the exact action fingerprint. The server now signs
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.01,0:01:08.61,Default,,0,0,0,,a short-lived passport. This is permission, not a delivery claim.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.00,0:01:15.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Changing the recipient invalidates the authorization. The original approved action
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.51,0:01:17.57,Default,,0,0,0,,remains available to execute.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.04,0:01:24.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Execute performs the work. The server writes actual document bytes into the
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.28,0:01:32.03,Default,,0,0,0,,recipient's local inbox, reads them back, verifies their SHA-256 hash, and persists
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.03,0:01:32.93,Default,,0,0,0,,this receipt.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.68,0:01:41.10,Default,,0,0,0,,A second execution is rejected. One human approval cannot be reused through another
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.10,0:01:42.44,Default,,0,0,0,,passport either.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.03,0:01:50.47,Default,,0,0,0,,After restarting the server, the receipt history is still here. Approval and replay
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.47,0:01:54.36,Default,,0,0,0,,records are durable, not just browser state.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.61,0:02:01.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The operator can also deny or revoke an action. A denial does not produce a usable
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.43,0:02:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,passport.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.53,0:02:11.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Six negative policy probes check forged approval, sensitive egress and unknown
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.80,0:02:18.03,Default,,0,0,0,,parameters. The demonstration also exercises real recipient tampering and replay.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.87,0:02:30.79,Default,,0,0,0,,The same Rust service exposes the governance explorer and MCP protocol 2025-11-25.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.79,0:02:35.41,Default,,0,0,0,,AIGON PROOF: approve the action, verify the outcome.
